#315 isn't finished: the image half is queued to land, but the workflow half (`.github/workflows/images.yml`) still can't be pushed, so the issue stays open.

**Why images.yml still can't land.** Jody granted the App `workflows: write`, but my checkpoint push with the images.yml change was refused with the same "without `workflows` permission" error. The cause is the looper's own token minting: `looper-token` asks GitHub for a fixed list of permissions. The report token's list (contents, issues, pull_requests, metadata) and the manager's (contents, issues, metadata) both leave out `workflows`. So neither my branch push nor the manager's push to main can include images.yml, whatever the App holds. I filed this as a bug: **tacplus-dev/looper#106**, asking to add `"workflows":"write"` to both lists.

**What's queued:**
- I resolved the `PROPOSALS.md` conflict by keeping both sets of entries. The images.yml entry now lists only the follow-ups: drop the buildx fallback, and run `just images` inside a build image.
- I committed the image half as `dd22c7ea` (rootless BuildKit, sccache, `tacplus-image-build`, `tacplus-cache`, the cold/warm determinism test, docs) and queued the land with the manager. Its verdict will come as a comment on the issue, and it lands even after this run ends.
- I applied the images.yml patch from the issue and actionlint passes on it. I then took it back out of the commit, since it would have made the land fail. The patch still applies cleanly to main.

**Checks:**
- The cache and image Go tests in `scripts` pass.
- The full `just gates` run didn't finish in this run. I stopped it after 3h15m, at the jwk-alg Rust leg, and it had no failures up to that point. The land runs the gates again.
- Rootless BuildKit itself and the identical cold/warm digests are still unproven. Both need unconfined seccomp and AppArmor, which a looper container doesn't get, so the first images.yml run on main will be the proof.
- This change touches no service handlers. `looper-trace check` reports 9 findings, all in the cross-test client driver this change doesn't touch, and #311 already tracks them.

I posted all of this on #315 and checkpointed the branch. The outcome file says `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/looper#106`. Once that's fixed, the next run applies the images.yml patch, lands it, checks its first run on main, and closes the issue.
